.TH QURAN-DETECT 1
.SH NAME
quran\-detect \- Detect Quran quotations in Arabic text and restore their canonical wording.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquran\-detect\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detect Quran quotations in Arabic text and restore their canonical wording.
.PP
Replace is the default command. Use identify to list quotations as JSON, plan to record every edit for an audit trail, and apply or revert to replay or undo a plan. Text comes from the embedded Tanzil Quran (Hafs, Kufan verse count).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBreplace\fR
Restore detected quotations to their canonical wording.
.TP
\fBidentify\fR
List detected quotations as a JSON array.
.TP
\fBplan\fR
Write a JSON plan of every edit without applying it.
.TP
\fBapply\fR
Apply or undo a saved plan.
.TP
\fBrevert\fR
Apply or undo a saved plan.
.TP
\fBcompletions\fR
Generate a completion script, or install it in the shell's user directory.
.TP
\fBspec\fR
Print the Usage specification as KDL for docs, man pages and tooling.
.SH "QURAN-DETECT REPLACE"
Restore detected quotations to their canonical wording.

Supply INPUT or \-\-text; a single dash reads UTF\-8 text from stdin. The restored text goes to stdout by default, with no added newline.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR quran\-detect replace [OPTIONS] [<INPUT>]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-text\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Direct text instead of INPUT; whitespace is kept exactly.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Destination file, or \- for stdout [default: stdout].
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing output file atomically, including INPUT if it is the destination.
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Aggressiveness preset; the options below override its individual values.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRbalanced
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-error\-fraction\fR \fI<F>\fR
Maximum alignment errors as a fraction of the passage length, from 0 to 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-edits\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum alignment errors in one quotation.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-words\fR \fI<N>\fR
Minimum canonical words in a quotation; at least 2.
.TP
\fB\-\-allowed\-errors\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated errors to allow: typo, missing, extra, join, split, substitution. An empty value allows none.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-exact\-context\fR \fI<WORDS>\fR
Exact words required around missing, extra or substituted words: N or BEFORE,AFTER. 0 disables the check.
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR \fI<SCRIPT>\fR
Spelling written into restored quotations; detection is the same for both.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRsimple\-plain
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-append\-reference\fR
Append a citation such as [البقرة \- ٢٥٥] after each quotation.
.TP
\fB\-\-brackets\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Brackets directly enclosing a quotation.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRkeep
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-matches\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Apply exactly the matches in this JSON file, as written by identify, instead of detecting. Keep any compatible subset in order; [] leaves the text unchanged.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<INPUT>\fR
A UTF\-8 text file, or \- for stdin.
\fBExit status:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success
.TP
\fB1\fR
Input, output, match or plan error
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid arguments
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Restore a text file
.PP
.RS 4
quran\-detect book.txt \-o book.restored.txt
.RE
.PP
Restore and cite
.PP
.RS 4
quran\-detect \-\-text 'قل هو الله احد' \-\-append\-reference
.RE
.PP
Apply only selected matches
.PP
.RS 4
quran\-detect book.txt \-\-matches chosen.json
.RE
